## 2. The WhatsApp-Style Incoming Call Architecture

To make a phone **ring suddenly** when the app is in the background or killed, we use OS-level VoIP and full-screen calling frameworks.

### 2.1 Android Architecture (Native Full-Screen Call)
- **Mechanism**: High-Priority Firebase Cloud Messaging (`priority: "high"`, `content_available: true`, `data`-only payload).
- **Foreground Telecom Integration**: Uses Android **`ConnectionService`** (Android Telecom Framework) or **`NotificationCompat.Builder.setFullScreenIntent()`**.
- **Behavior**:
  - Wakes up the device CPU from Doze mode.
  - Bypasses screen lock and shows full-screen incoming call UI.
  - Plays continuous ringtone via `STREAM_RING` (vibration + sound).
  - Displays Caller Name ("District Collector Alok Sharma"), Designation, and Hearing Subject.
  - Action buttons: **Accept (Green)** and **Decline (Red)**.
  - If answered, launches the LiveKit room directly without asking for password/PIN.

### 2.2 iOS Architecture (Apple CallKit)
- **Mechanism**: Apple **`PushKit`** (VoIP Push Notifications).
- **Framework**: **`CallKit`** integration (`CXProvider`).
- **Behavior**:
  - Triggers the native iOS system incoming call screen (identical to a regular cellular or WhatsApp call).
  - Shows custom caller name ("Jan Sunwai: District Collector").
  - Seamless audio routing and system-level lock screen call answering.
  - When unlocked/answered, transitions directly into the LiveKit video view.

### 2.3 Web App Incoming Ringing (WhatsApp Web Style)
- When an Officer or Employee is logged into the web portal (`web.jansunwai.rajasthan.gov.in`):
  - Connected via persistent secure **WebSocket**.
  - On incoming call signal, web browser plays a loud ringing audio loop (Web Audio API).
  - Displays full-screen modal with ringing animation, caller profile, and Accept/Reject buttons.

